## 2. Mutations of my own — eight, against the pinned assertion

Harness: a script that edits real files in the scratch, runs usage.test.ts,
reverts in a `finally` and asserts `git diff --quiet` after every case.
Kept at $TMPDIR/w030r3-mutations.mjs and $TMPDIR/w030r3-mut2.mjs (scratch,
not committed — this is the reviewer's probe, not the opus's evidence).

  N1  ONE constant annotated `: string` (round 1's own survivor)
      CAUGHT  exit 1   seen=29
  N2  N1 PLUS one duplicated banner line added to another constant
      SURVIVED exit 0  seen=30                             <- see §5, the ceiling
  N3  one constant converted to a template literal
      CAUGHT  exit 1   seen=29
  N4  one constant renamed off the `*_USAGE` convention
      CAUGHT  exit 1   seen=29
  N5' constant renamed out of BOTH the `*_USAGE`/`USAGE_*` prefixes
      CAUGHT  exit 1   seen=29
  N6  INFLATION probe — a decoy `DECOY_USAGE` whose text is already a banner
      line, added to pad the scan
      CAUGHT  exit 1   seen=31
  N7  a `;` inside the literal, breaking the non-greedy declaration regex
      CAUGHT  exit 1   seen=29
  N8  a banner line deleted from USAGE, its constant left alone
      CAUGHT  exit 1   seen=30 but FAIL on prune.ts:PRUNE_USAGE's line
  N9  a banner line with NO backing constant drifts (`check`)
      SURVIVED exit 0                                      <- declared out of scope

The task asked specifically whether `seen` can be inflated by a false-positive
scan. N6 answers it: it can be inflated, and inflation fails the assertion
exactly as deflation does (31 != 30). A decoy cannot be used to pad the count
back to 30 after knocking a real constant out — it overshoots. Only an exactly
compensating edit survives (N2).

N1 is the one that matters for the round-2 finding: the OLD `sawAny` guard
survived 21 constants dropping out; the new pin fails on ONE. That is the
whole class, not the M13 instance, and I verified it directly.

N9 is A3, already named in the brief's Out of scope as of this PR: `check`,
`init`, `context`, `query` have no backing constant and can drift. Honest
limit of a scoped feature, unchanged ruling from round 2.

